    "explanation": "Both of you: the money in dispute is the 5.00 SGD no-show cancellation fee charged to the rider at 09:51:29 on 14 Aug 2026 (EV-FARE-05054, cancellation_fee 5.00, total_charged 5.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The rider filed, contesting it. I find the rider is right, and the fee is returned in full.\n\nWhy: this was an on-demand trip with no scheduled pickup time, so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait runs from the driver's arrival. The platform's own trip record (EV-TRIP-05054) puts arrival at 09:47:05 and the driver's cancellation at 09:51:25 — 260 seconds later — and its own free_wait flag reads cancelled_after_free_wait = false. The free wait therefore ran to 09:52:05 and the driver cancelled 40 seconds before it expired. POL-NS-22 charges the 5.00 SGD fee only 'when the driver cancels after the free wait'. That condition was not met, so the fee was not earned and the rider should not carry it. POL-GEN-03's FULL_REFUND applies: the filing rider is right on the whole contested amount, so 5.00 SGD is returned and driver_compensation_sgd is null.\n\nWhat I did not accept from the driver's side: the driver argues POL-NS-21 is only a permission and that nothing but POL-NS-23 voids the fee. It is true the driver was at the pickup — the GPS trace (EV-GPS-05054) corroborates the 09:47:05 arrival, nearest qualifying fix 2.73 m away at 4 m reported accuracy, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius and 25 m filter — and it is true the POL-NS-23 contact obligation was met (two in-app messages at 09:47:30 and 09:49:50, both read, and one in-app call at 09:50:30 ringing 22 s unanswered, all before cancelled_at 09:51:25). But the charging condition in POL-NS-22 is the free wait, not arrival and not contact; contact is a separate cumulative protection, and meeting it does not license a cancellation made before the wait expires. POL-NS-24 gives the rider nothing, because the driver did arrive.\n\nWhat I did not need from the rider's side: POL-GEN-26 escalation is