    "explanation": "Outcome: the 5.00 SGD no-show fee is refunded to you in full, with no driver compensation and no referrals.\n\nTo the rider: your point about the five-minute wait decides this. This was an on-demand trip, so under POL-NS-21 the driver's free wait of 300 seconds ran from his arrival at 09:47:05 and did not expire until 09:52:05. The trip record (EV-TRIP-05054) puts the cancellation at 09:51:25 - 260 seconds after arrival, 40 seconds short - and its own flag free_wait.cancelled_after_free_wait is false. The 09:47:05 arrival is independently corroborated by the GPS trace (EV-GPS-05054): the nearest fix sits 2.73 m from the pickup with a reported accuracy of 4 m, inside the 25 m accuracy filter and the 50 m STANDARD radius. POL-NS-22 charges a no-show fee only 'when the driver cancels after the free wait', and POL-NS-21 lets a driver cancel 'as a rider no-show' only after the free wait. That condition was not met, so the 5.00 SGD charged at 09:51:29 (EV-FARE-05054) was not earned and the whole contested amount is returned. The record carries no rider track, so I do not rely on your account of walking down; the fee's invalidity stands on the driver's own timestamps.\n\nTo the driver: I accept that you arrived at the pickup and that your contact obligation under POL-NS-23 was met - two in-app messages (09:47:30 and 09:49:50) and one unanswered in-app call (09:50:30), all before the 09:51:25 cancellation, and the trace shows you stationary at the kerb. But POL-NS-23 is one requirement of the fee, not the whole of its basis: POL-NS-22 makes the fee depend on cancelling after the free wait, and you cancelled 40 seconds before it expired. Your statement that you 'waited more than 5 minutes' is not borne out by your own record.\n\nNo escalation: POL-GEN-26 is not engaged. Every fact the no-show rules need - arrival, cancellation, contact and the charge - is carried by COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0, and the only absence is the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05054-01, a MISSING artifact at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, which carries no fact and which no no-show rule turns on.\n\nNo referrals: POL-NS-22's referral fires only where the amount charged differs from 5.00 SGD and the record charged exactly 5.00; POL-NS-24's goodwill credit applies only where the driver also failed to attempt contact, and contact was attempted; POL-NS-25's repeat no-show flag needs a count of 3 or more, the profile does not carry that field, and the fee does not stand in any event.\n\nConfidence: the deciding facts (arrival and cancellation times) are carried by EV-TRIP-05054 and EV-GPS-05054, both weight 1.0, so the cap is 1.00. At 5.00 SGD, with no fraud flags on either profile, the AI ruling on this no-show is final (POL-GEN-22, POL-NS-26)."
